BitBlt comment:
'I represent the transfer of bits from one rectangle within a Form (source form) to another (destination form). The transfer is carried out with respect to a halftone form that serves as a mask for combining bits. Halftones are 16x16-bit forms which are repeated indefinitely as needed by the BitBlt method. If the source form is not specified, then the halftone is taken by itself to be the source. This can be used for filling an area with a constant pattern. The result of the transfer is stored according to a combination rule which specifies one of 16 ways to combine the source, destination, and halftone mask form. Also the store is clipped within a specified rectangular area.'!

