Etherworld comment:
'This is, of course, the class that controls all of the basic Ethernet operations. There should not be more than one instance of Etherworld, and one, Ether, has to be defined for the system to work.  

In this implementation, and due to timing considerations, it is expected that the transmitter will post quite quickly; thus, we disable interrupts and busy wait for its completion.

In general, the interrupt is only armed when we have started the receiver. Etherworld currently uses these input processes in the ProcessorScheduler: 
	IntProc		A Process at IntProcLevel; awakened when the device interrupts.
	InputProc	A Process at InputProcLevel; distributes packets to sockets,
				allowing each socket to then run.

Note that some of the timers may be on other levels.

The Ethernet can be in one of several states:
	if Ether == nil, there is nothing.
	if Ether ~~ nil, etherState can be EthAwake, EthAsleep, or EthDead:
		EthDead	Ether created and class initialization done, but nothing else.
		EthAsleep	Ether data structures created, but no attempt to start.
		EthAwake	Ether is up and running.

The messages wakeup, sleep, and kill move to one of those states.
Other messages are used for single transitions from adjacent states.

If you just want to temporarily prevent the device from running use etherStop and etherStart.
Should go to EthAsleep (use Ether sleep) if you quit, since may come up on a different machine.

The lights on the right side of the screen are Etherworld signals. They mean Etherworld awakened; packet addressed to the Alto received; packet being processed; output being sent; and input rejected.
'!

!Etherworld methodsFor: 'initialize-release'!etherStart
	"Allows Ether to start running again"

	EtherState = EthAwake
		ifTrue: 
			["Kicks the device"
			self SIO: 3 signal: (IntSemActive _ IntSem)
			"Forces it to wake up again"]
		ifFalse: 
			[self notify: 'Attempt to etherStart when not awake!!!!.']!etherStop
	"Temporarily shuts off the Ether"

	self SIO: 3 signal: (IntSemActive _ nil)!Init
	"Move Ether from state EthDead to EthAsleep"
	"If we were already running, bring it all down, Just in case!!!!!!"

	EtherState = EthDead ifFalse: [self kill "now sure we are EthDead"].
	NETNUM _ HOSTNUM _ 0. "may get reset later"
	self setLights.
	JustArrivedQ _ SharedQueue new.
	EthInPacNext _ Pacbuf new.
	SocketProtect _ Semaphore forMutualExclusion.
	SocketTable _ Dictionary new: 16.
	RoutingTable _ ByteArray new: 255 withAll: 0.
	"1-255, 0 is special"
	RoutingHopCount _ ByteArray new: 255 withAll: 8.
	RoutingUpdateUser _ RoutingUpdater new init.
	IntProcLevel _ Processor highIOPriority.
	InputProcLevel _ Processor lowIOPriority.
	self installIntProc.
	self installInputProc.
	EtherState _ EthAsleep
	"We are still asleep, must do a wakeup to get numbers, start, etc."!kill
	"Shuts down ethernet and PUP world completely"

	| socket |
	EtherState = EthDead
		ifFalse: 
			["Should free up all of the storage, etc..... 
			Would need to wakeup or Init, to get started again. 
			Device may have been running"
			"Do nothing"
			EtherState = EthAwake ifTrue: [self sleep].
			SocketProtect critical: [SocketTable do: [:socket | socket kill]].
			self SIO: 3 signal: (IntSemActive _ nil).
			"Disable signal"
			IntSem _ IntSemActive _ nil.
			"Discard semaphores (and processes)"
			InputProc == nil ifFalse: [InputProc terminate. InputProc _ nil].
			EthInPacNext _ nil.
			"Release the queue to avoid circular data structures"
			JustArrivedQ ~= nil ifTrue: [JustArrivedQ release. JustArrivedQ _ nil].
			RoutingUpdateUser == nil ifFalse: [RoutingUpdateUser release].
			RoutingUpdateUser _ RoutingTable _ RoutingHopCount _ nil.
			EtherState _ EthDead]!release
	"Do this when quitting. Make asleep if awake."

	EtherState = EthAwake ifTrue: [self sleep]!setLights
	| right |
	right _ Display width.
	IntLight _ BitBlt toReverse: (Rectangle origin: (right - 32) @ 0 extent: 16 @ 16).
	InputLight _ BitBlt toReverse: (Rectangle origin: (right - 16) @ 0 extent: 16 @ 16).
	OutputLight _ BitBlt toReverse: (Rectangle origin: (right - 32) @ 16 extent: 16 @ 16)!sleep
	"Be sure to do this before a user quit"

	| socket |
	EtherState = EthDead
		ifTrue: [self Init]
		ifFalse:
			["That is, go from dead to asleep"
			EtherState = EthAsleep
				ifFalse:
					["Already asleep"
					EtherState = EthAwake
						ifTrue:
							[SocketProtect critical:
								[SocketTable do: "try to shut down gracefully"
									[:socket | socket sleep]]. "warn the sockets, leaves them in table"
							self etherStop.
							EtherState _ EthAsleep
							"When next we wake up, may be on a new machine/net"]]]!wakeup
	"Try to get everything up and running"

	| socket |
	EtherState = EthAwake
		ifTrue: [self etherStart]
		ifFalse:
			["Do nothing, kick the receiver"
			EtherState = EthDead
				ifTrue: [self sleep].
			EtherState = EthAsleep
				ifTrue:
					[HOSTNUM _ self getMachineID
					"This is the tricky one, need to get our machine # and routing table.
					May have come up on a different network and host, assume the worst".
					self setMachineID: HOSTNUM.
					NETNUM _ 0.
					SocketProtect critical:
						[SocketTable do: [:socket | socket setOutAddBlock]].
					EtherState _ EthAwake.
					self etherStart.
					RoutingUpdateUser update.
					NETNUM = 0
					ifTrue: [EtherState _ EthAsleep. self error: 'no routing tables']
					ifFalse:
						["Tell leftover sockets current net&host, and that we are awake again"
						SocketProtect critical:
							[SocketTable do:
								[:socket | socket setOutAddBlock. socket wakeup]]]]
				ifFalse:
					[self notify: 'In wakeup, found Ethernet in some unknown state.']]! !
!Etherworld methodsFor: 'input interrupt routines'!copyinput: buffer
	"Copy the most recent incoming packet into the first argument (a packet buffer).  Fail if the buffer is a pointer containing object or if it is not big enough for a full sized PUP.  Xerox specific primitive.  See Object whatIsAPrimitive."

	<primitive: 131>
	self primitiveFailed!installInputProc
	| inBuf destSoc |
	InputProc _ [[true] whileTrue:
		["Infinite loop for process in scheduler"
		inBuf _ JustArrivedQ next.
		InputLight destForm: Display; copyBits; destForm: nil.
		"Process each incoming buffer, know it's a PUP" "verify the incoming checksum"
		(CheckIncomingCS and: [inBuf checksumOK == false])
			ifFalse:
				["To be honest, we should check the destNet and destHost,
				but they generally have to be OK..... OK to pass the packet on"
				(destSoc _ self socketNumber: inBuf destSocNum) notNil
					ifTrue: [destSoc acceptPacbuf: inBuf].
				"Couldn't find a socket for it, done"].
		InputLight destForm: Display; copyBits; destForm: nil "last action in the loop"]]
	 newProcess.
	InputProc priority: InputProcLevel.
	InputProc resume!installIntProc
	IntSem _ Semaphore new.
	[[true] whileTrue:
		["Infinite loop for process in scheduler.
		Interrupt just happened, running at a high level, interface off.
		Something just happened, do the common cases first.
		Input is wired down below; only comes here if OK.
		Note: we can only come here if last action was to start the rec!!!!"
		"Copy out the packet first."
		IntSem wait.
		IntLight destForm: Display; copyBits.
		EthInPacNext == nil ifTrue: [EthInPacNext _ Pacbuf new init].
		self copyinput: EthInPacNext pupString.
		"Start the receiver."
		self SIO: 2 signal: IntSem.
		JustArrivedQ nextPut: EthInPacNext "now process this input".
		EthInPacNext _ Pacbuf new.
		IntLight copyBits; destForm: nil "last action in the loop"]]
	 forkAt: IntProcLevel! !
!Etherworld methodsFor: 'output routines'!doOutput: buffer words: words
	"Broadcast the contents of the packet buffer over the Ethernet.  Fail if words is not an Integer or is larger than the buffer length.  Xerox specific primitive.  See Object whatIsAPrimitive."

	<primitive: 133>
	self primitiveFailed!sendOutput: ethOutPac
	 "This is the one and only place from which we send output. Only one packet gets passed in to us at a time. For performance, we wait here for the transmitter to post!!!!!!!! Nominally, we are running at level 0; thus, this must be run at a Top critical, to protect from multiple calls. There is a special check for sending a packet to ourselves, which the hardware does not support."

	| post pac |
	EtherState ~= EthAwake ifTrue:
		[self wakeup. Transcript show: 'Starting Ethernet...'].
	OutputLight destForm: Display; copyBits.
	(ethOutPac imEthDestHost = HOSTNUM and: [ethOutPac destNet = NETNUM])
		ifTrue: "Sending to ourselves, just put the packet on the input queue"
			[pac _ Pacbuf new. "Copy in case client is hanging on to it"
			pac pupStringGet: ethOutPac pupString copy.
			JustArrivedQ nextPut: pac]
		ifFalse:
			[(post _ self doOutput: ethOutPac pupString words: ethOutPac totLengthWords) ~= 511
				ifTrue:
					[Transcript cr; show: 'Warning, bad output post: ', (post radix: 8)]].
	OutputLight copyBits; destForm: nil! !
!Etherworld methodsFor: 'user messages'!awake
	^EtherState = EthAwake!broadcastFilter: value
	value
		ifTrue:	[BroadcastFilter _ true. self broadcastFilterSet: 1]
		ifFalse:	[BroadcastFilter _ false. self broadcastFilterSet: 0]!broadcastFilterSet: value
	"Order the hardware to accept braodcast packets (value = 0) or reject them (value = 1).  Xerox specific primitive.  See Object whatIsAPrimitive."

